message.content:
I found two likely periapical lesions, both graded PAI 3. My confidence in both is low to moderate. I checked the image with zoomed and contrast-enhanced crops.

1. **Lower first molar on the image's left (patient's right), the root-canal-filled tooth with the large restoration and post.** There is a faint area of mineral loss around the root tips, mostly near the distal root. The edges are not well defined, so I graded it PAI 3 rather than 4.
2. **Upper central incisor with the post.** There is a little dense material just above the root tip, which may be extruded root canal filling. The bone right around the tip looks diffusely darker, but this may partly be the nasal and incisive canal structures overlapping it. Graded PAI 3.

The upper molar on the image's right (patient's left) with the crown and root canal fillings was the third candidate. I did not include it because I could not see a clear radiolucent area at its root tips.

